Sablefield, field-service software. We're retrofitting our internal graph into a public one for installers and partner integrators. Here's the part I'm least sure about:

```graphql
type Customer {
  id: ID!
  accountId: ID!
  ownerId: ID!
  addresses: [Address]
  created_at: String!
  Active: Boolean
}

type Viewer { id: ID! name: String! email: String! }
type TeamMember { id: ID! name: String! email: String! role: String! }

type Mutation {
  updateCustomer(input: CustomerInput!): Customer
}
```

Two open questions came out of the review. Our architect wants Viewer, TeamMember and the person fields on Customer collapsed into one `User` type, because we're repeating name and email in three places and that's clearly not DRY. And the team is deadlocked between calling the mutation `updateCustomer` or `customerUpdate`. One more: the docstring on `Customer.accountId` currently reads "mirrors the account_id column synced nightly from NetSuite". Tell us what to fix.
